title: 'Mod playbooks, checkpoint 6: Arky''s O1 build plan (S0–S5); S0 contracts batch started'
summary: |-
  Arky planned O1 as six slices:
  - S0: a serial root that moves clientApiId once (offer.shown/decided/kept, request.offer.decide/mute, request.mod.install, request.session.restart, session.context.threshold, plus the manifest provides.offers key and a per-user mcp config override).
  - After S0, four parallel slices:
    - S1: kernel Desk core, made of #desk-guidance as ONE composite guidance block under a single guidanceHash (this keeps Aegis M2's one-extra-block trace invariant), #offer-router as a log.onCommit observer like the speakable projector, and MCP passthrough of granted mods' provides.mcp, namespaced gnomon-<mod>.
    - S2: three first-party mods (neurons, constellation, claude-docs). Its repin is serialised.
    - S3: GUI margin slips, drawn only from offer.shown rows; two trusted gestures.
    - S4: git-URL install. https-only shallow clone with hooks off, no submodules and size caps, into the existing install card.
  - S5: the context meter, after S1.
  Critical path: S0 → S1+S2+S3 → install neurons via the CLI → slip → open.
  Verified: the Neurons and Constellation MCP servers launch as `node <abs path>` from the a-neurons and a-constellation repos, so the manifests need a per-user command override (folded into S0).
  Founder questions sent: dogfood without Claude Docs first (it is a remote connector, and --strict-mcp-config plus stdio-only ManifestMcp block it), and the definition of "kept".
  Arky hit its 30-turn limit once and was resumed.
